---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Brighter Sites | Therapist Website Design"
  description="Brighter Sites builds thoughtful, professional websites for therapists and counseling practices with design, usability, analytics, and search visibility in mind."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Brighter Sites</p>

      <h1>
        It started with one counseling practice that needed a better kind of website.
      </h1>

      <p class="page-lead">
        Brighter Sites grew out of the process of building a website for a new
        counseling practice from the ground up—one that needed to feel calm,
        professional, inviting, and genuinely useful to the people visiting it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-story">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Where it started</p>
        <h2>More than putting a practice online.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>
          The first goal was straightforward: create a website that gave
          prospective clients a clear sense of the practice before they ever
          made contact.
        </p>

        <p>
          That meant making it easy to understand who the counselor works with,
          the concerns they support, the approaches they use, what the practice
          feels like, and how someone can take the next step.
        </p>

        <p>
          But as the site developed, it became clear that the public-facing
          design was only one part of the job.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The other half of the website</p>

        <h2>
          A beautiful site should also work hard behind the scenes.
        </h2>

        <p>
          A therapy website should not simply exist. It should be structured
          thoughtfully, load well, provide useful information to search engines,
          and give the practice a way to understand how people are finding and
          using it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Thoughtful search structure</h3>
          <p>
            Clear service pages, useful page titles, understandable URLs, and
            technically sound site structure help search engines understand what
            the practice offers and where it serves clients.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Useful analytics</h3>
          <p>
            Website analytics can show which pages people visit, how they move
            through the site, and which parts of the site are actually helping
            generate interest in the practice.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <h3>Cost-conscious growth</h3>
          <p>
            Good structure, useful content, performance, and organic search
            visibility can help a practice build traffic over time without
            depending entirely on paid advertising.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-story">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why Brighter Sites</p>
        <h2>That experience became the model.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>
          Brighter Sites was created around that same idea: the website should
          represent the practice well to the people who see it while also being
          built intelligently underneath.
        </p>

        <p>
          Design, mobile usability, page structure, technical performance,
          analytics, search visibility, and ongoing cost all matter. None of
          those pieces should be treated as an afterthought.
        </p>

        <p>
          The goal is not to promise a particular Google ranking or fill a site
          with search-engine tricks. It is to give therapy practices a strong
          technical and content foundation that gives them the best reasonable
          opportunity to be discovered organically.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">The result</p>

        <h2>
          A site clients can trust and a practice can grow with.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Brighter Sites combines thoughtful design with the technical pieces
          that help a counseling website remain useful long after launch.
        </p>

        <a class="button" href="/contact/">
          Start a project
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
